Local patches:
- patches/0001-pluggable-main-window-finder.patch — tabtabtab_nuke_core.py gets
  set_main_window_finder(fn) and _find_main_window(), used at the three
  _find_nuke_main_window() call sites, so a non-Nuke host (Natron) can plug
  in its own main-window lookup; _find_nuke_main_window itself and Nuke's
  behaviour are unchanged.
- patches/0002-host-row-metrics.patch — tabtabtab_nuke_core.py gets
  set_row_metrics(row_height, visible_rows), used by TabTabTabWidget in
  place of the hardcoded "twice the font height" row and 18 visible rows,
  so a host can size the popup to its own row height; defaults are
  unchanged, so Nuke's sizing is untouched. The popup's placement is
  upstream's, unchanged.
- patches/0003-refresh-retained-row-menuobj.patch — tabtabtab_nuke_core.py's
  NodeModel._apply_items keeps a visually unchanged row's dict as before
  (still no dataChanged), but now swaps in the refresh's menuobj and, when
  it is a different object, drops the row's cached colour. Without it a
  host that builds fresh handles per refresh (Natron: per-project QActions,
  node entries carrying the current category colour) kept invoking and
  colouring from the first open's handles. Re-filtering on a keystroke
  reuses the same menuobjs, so Nuke's per-keystroke cost is unchanged.
  tests/test_node_model_diff.py gains two tests for it.
- 0004 (no patch file; see git history) — tabtabtab_nuke_core.py's
  TabTabTabWidget refreshes its items synchronously before it shows, and
  only when get_items() returns a different list or the weights changed
  (NodeWeights gains version, dirty and a file mtime check, so a weights
  file written elsewhere is reloaded), instead of deferring a full refresh
  to the next event-loop tick after showing. close() no longer writes the
  weights: a single-shot timer saves them a second later, and
  flush_weights() saves any not yet written. create() asks the plugin's
  new invoke_opens_window(thing) hook (default True): when it says False,
  the choice is invoked before the popup closes, otherwise after, as
  before. create() no longer sets the input to the choice's name; the
  next show does, with the input's signals blocked, and filters once as
  part of its refresh (NodeModel.refresh_items takes the filter text).
  set_weights_file() repoints the weights.
  A host whose get_items() builds a new list per call refreshes on every
  open, as before.
- tests/test_host_hooks.py is a new test file, added by Natron (not from
  upstream), covering set_main_window_finder(), _find_main_window(),
  set_row_metrics(), _row_height() and _visible_rows().
- tests/test_create_order.py is a new test file, added by Natron, covering
  create()'s invoke/close order and the deferred pre-fill on the next show.
